{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/a2-everyday-australia-part-2/audio/main-1b555bbd40ed.mp3","durationSec":316.2,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":3.16,"text":"Canberra is the capital of Australia, and it is a planned city."},{"start":3.9,"end":6.82,"text":"People drew the city on paper first, and then they built it."},{"start":7.06,"end":7.26,"text":"Why?"},{"start":8.18,"end":14.54,"text":"When Australia became one country, Sydney and Melbourne both wanted to be the capital."},{"start":15.2,"end":16.08,"text":"They could not agree."},{"start":16.7,"end":18.94,"text":"So the government built a new city between them."},{"start":19.66,"end":23.94,"text":"Two Americans, a husband and wife, won a competition to draw the new city."},{"start":24.6,"end":28.52,"text":"They were Walter Burley Griffin and Marion Mahony Griffin."},{"start":29.24,"end":32.16,"text":"For the Griffins, a lake was the heart of the city."},{"start":32.82,"end":33.42,"text":"Why a lake?"},{"start":34.04,"end":36.12,"text":"The river was in low land between hills."},{"start":36.88,"end":41.16,"text":"Water could fill this low land easily and cheaply, and a lake would be beautiful."},{"start":41.98,"end":44.62,"text":"So the Griffins drew the city around it."},{"start":44.96,"end":47.58,"text":"But Canberra had only a small river."},{"start":48.02,"end":51.48,"text":"So workers built a dam, a big wall that stops a river."},{"start":52.3,"end":55.68,"text":"In 1963, they closed its gates."},{"start":56.02,"end":60.42,"text":"The river water stopped at the wall, and slowly it made a lake."},{"start":61.46,"end":63.24,"text":"Its name is Lake Burley Griffin."},{"start":64.24,"end":66.3,"text":"Today the lake is the weekend park for the city."},{"start":66.86,"end":69.58,"text":"People walk or ride bikes on the bridge-to-bridge loop."},{"start":70.04,"end":71.68,"text":"It is a 5-kilometre circle."},{"start":72.1,"end":73.32,"text":"It goes over two bridges."},{"start":74.22,"end":77.26,"text":"Rowing clubs train in long, thin boats at the west end."},{"start":77.26,"end":81.14,"text":"Families cook lunch on the free electric barbecues by the water."},{"start":81.84,"end":85.82,"text":"A sausage sizzle is a barbecue that sells food to raise money for a group."},{"start":86.58,"end":88.78,"text":"Sizzle is the sound of food cooking on a hot plate."},{"start":89.36,"end":91.44,"text":"You get one sausage in a slice of white bread."},{"start":92.12,"end":94.46,"text":"Many people add fried onions and tomato sauce."},{"start":95.2,"end":98.72,"text":"The most famous ones are outside Bunnings, a big hardware shop."},{"start":99.28,"end":102.48,"text":"A hardware shop sells tools and things for your house and garden."},{"start":103.22,"end":106.9,"text":"On weekends, a local group, like a school or a sports club, cooks there."},{"start":107.4,"end":110.12,"text":"Bunnings takes no money from the group, so the group keeps it all."},{"start":110.62,"end":112.54,"text":"A sausage costs $3.50."},{"start":113.32,"end":117.56,"text":"Sausage sizzles also appear on election day, the day people vote."},{"start":118.06,"end":121.18,"text":"They are at polling places, the places where people vote."},{"start":121.98,"end":122.42,"text":"Why there?"},{"start":123.32,"end":125.18,"text":"In Australia, voting is compulsory."},{"start":126.1,"end":129.74,"text":"Every Australian citizen aged 18 or older must vote."},{"start":130.6,"end":132.82,"text":"People who do not vote can get a fine."},{"start":133.64,"end":136.12,"text":"A fine is money you pay when you break a rule."},{"start":136.66,"end":140.88,"text":"Because of this law, more than 90% of people vote in national elections."},{"start":140.88,"end":145.12,"text":"Elections are on Saturdays, and people often vote in schools."},{"start":146.12,"end":149.46,"text":"Almost everyone comes, so school parents cook for the long lines."},{"start":149.92,"end":151.18,"text":"The money helps the school."},{"start":151.18,"end":153.98,"text":"Australians call this a democracy sausage."},{"start":154.98,"end":157.92,"text":"In a democracy, people choose their leaders by voting."},{"start":158.92,"end":162.04,"text":"The Melbourne Cup is the most famous horse race in Australia."},{"start":162.76,"end":165.34,"text":"In a race, horses run to see who is fastest."},{"start":166.02,"end":168.68,"text":"People call this one the race that stops a nation."},{"start":169.34,"end":172.94,"text":"For a few minutes, almost all of Australia stops to watch."},{"start":173.58,"end":177.62,"text":"When: the first Tuesday in November, at 3 pm."},{"start":177.62,"end":180.36,"text":"Where: Flemington Racecourse in Melbourne."},{"start":181.24,"end":184.36,"text":"How long: 3,200 metres."},{"start":184.36,"end":186.68,"text":"Why does all of Australia stop for one race?"},{"start":187.56,"end":191.34,"text":"Cup Day is a public holiday in Victoria, the state where Melbourne is."},{"start":191.66,"end":193,"text":"People there do not go to work."},{"start":193.32,"end":195.94,"text":"They go to the race, or they watch it on TV with friends."},{"start":196.56,"end":199.38,"text":"In other states, Cup Day is a normal work day."},{"start":199.84,"end":202.14,"text":"But many offices stop at 3 pm."},{"start":202.14,"end":203.98,"text":"People watch the race together on TV."},{"start":204.62,"end":206.26,"text":"Many offices also have a sweep."},{"start":206.9,"end":208.26,"text":"It is a small game for the race."},{"start":208.68,"end":210.98,"text":"Everyone pays the same, often a few dollars."},{"start":211.64,"end":213.98,"text":"Each person takes a horse's name from a hat."},{"start":214.6,"end":217.6,"text":"The person with the winning horse gets about half of the money."},{"start":218.14,"end":219.76,"text":"You do not need to know about horses."},{"start":220.22,"end":223.72,"text":"It is all luck, so everyone in the office has a horse to cheer for."},{"start":225.6,"end":229.12,"text":"In 2026, a horse called Point Of Law won."},{"start":229.66,"end":231.447,"text":"Its trainer was Ciaron Maher."},{"start":231.447,"end":233.66,"text":"A trainer gets a horse ready for races."},{"start":233.66,"end":237.44,"text":"Ciaron Maher also trained the horses in second and third place."},{"start":237.98,"end":240.72,"text":"This was the first time in 166 races."},{"start":241.32,"end":243.18,"text":"One trainer had the first three horses."},{"start":245.2,"end":245.58,"text":"No tips."},{"start":246.12,"end":249,"text":"In cafés and restaurants, people do not usually leave a tip."},{"start":249.44,"end":251.72,"text":"A tip is a little money for the person who serves you."},{"start":252.08,"end":252.32,"text":"Why?"},{"start":252.32,"end":254.74,"text":"Australian workers already get high pay."},{"start":255.16,"end":257.44,"text":"So they do not need tips to make enough money."},{"start":257.44,"end":260.76,"text":"The lowest pay the law allows is called the minimum wage."},{"start":261.32,"end":266.8,"text":"From 1 July 2026, it is $26.44 an hour for adults."},{"start":267.42,"end":270.24,"text":"The Fair Work Commission decides this number every year."},{"start":270.24,"end":271.84,"text":"Super."},{"start":271.84,"end":276.56,"text":"Every boss must also pay 12% of a worker's pay into a super fund."},{"start":277.32,"end":279.74,"text":"Super is short for superannuation."},{"start":280.18,"end":282.78,"text":"The fund keeps this money until you are old."},{"start":283.48,"end":283.68,"text":"Why?"},{"start":284.2,"end":286.62,"text":"So people have their own money when they stop work."},{"start":287.86,"end":290.82,"text":"The rule changed on 1 July 2026."},{"start":291.66,"end":294.88,"text":"Now the boss pays super with every payday, the day you get your pay."},{"start":296.36,"end":297.36,"text":"Long service leave."},{"start":297.96,"end":301.92,"text":"After 10 years with the same company, workers get long service leave."},{"start":302.4,"end":304.94,"text":"It is a long holiday, and you still get your pay."},{"start":305.7,"end":309.02,"text":"In New South Wales, the state where Sydney is, it is two months."},{"start":309.8,"end":311.2,"text":"Other states have different rules."},{"start":311.84,"end":312.02,"text":"Why?"},{"start":312.66,"end":315.8,"text":"It is a thank-you for staying with one company for a long time."}],"words":[{"text":"Canberra","start":0,"end":0.32},{"text":"is","start":0.32,"end":0.54},{"text":"the","start":0.54,"end":0.66},{"text":"capital","start":0.66,"end":0.94},{"text":"of","start":0.94,"end":1.14},{"text":"Australia","start":1.14,"end":1.52},{"text":"and","start":1.52,"end":2.12},{"text":"it","start":2.12,"end":2.22},{"text":"is","start":2.22,"end":2.32},{"text":"a","start":2.32,"end":2.46},{"text":"planned","start":2.46,"end":2.76},{"text":"city","start":2.76,"end":3.16},{"text":"People","start":3.9,"end":4.08},{"text":"drew","start":4.08,"end":4.28},{"text":"the","start":4.28,"end":4.46},{"text":"city","start":4.46,"end":4.62},{"text":"on","start":4.62,"end":4.8},{"text":"paper","start":4.8,"end":5.06},{"text":"first","start":5.06,"end":5.48},{"text":"and","start":5.48,"end":5.96},{"text":"then","start":5.96,"end":6.06},{"text":"they","start":6.06,"end":6.2},{"text":"built","start":6.2,"end":6.38},{"text":"it","start":6.38,"end":6.82},{"text":"Why","start":7.06,"end":7.26},{"text":"When","start":8.18,"end":8.26},{"text":"Australia","start":8.26,"end":8.82},{"text":"became","start":8.82,"end":9.36},{"text":"one","start":9.36,"end":9.74},{"text":"country","start":9.74,"end":10.28},{"text":"Sydney","start":10.8,"end":10.98},{"text":"and","start":10.98,"end":11.36},{"text":"Melbourne","start":11.36,"end":11.82},{"text":"both","start":11.82,"end":12.66},{"text":"wanted","start":12.66,"end":13.32},{"text":"to","start":13.32,"end":13.6},{"text":"be","start":13.6,"end":13.82},{"text":"the","start":13.82,"end":14.14},{"text":"capital","start":14.14,"end":14.54},{"text":"They","st